  "title": "Aleph Alpha releases Kolibri-1",
  "narration": "Germany just dropped a 78-billion-parameter AI model that only wakes up 3.46 billion parameters per token. Kolibri-1 is Aleph Alpha's new open-weight bilingual model, built for German and English reasoning, coding, tool use, and long documents. The trick is mixture-of-experts: most of the model stays asleep while six routed experts work each token. That saves compute, not memory; the FP8 weights still need about 78 gigabytes. Aleph Alpha says context can stretch to one million tokens, though it recommends 262K for efficiency. So yes, the hummingbird is huge. It just flaps selectively.",
